{"availability":"available","full":"COVESA/ifex","name":"ifex","description":"The Interface Exchange Framework.   Tools for processing interface/API descriptions in different formats, including the IFEX core format.  Documentation in the README below and http://covesa.github.io/ifex/","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":24,"forks":24,"created":"2020-07-14T18:49:58Z","updated":"2026-08-20T15:03:51Z","license":"MPL-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://covesa.github.io/ifex-viewer/playground/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.476Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.476Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.476Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.476Z","stars":24,"forks":24}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["...for the the Interface Exchange framework (IFEX).","IFEX is a general interface description and transformation technology to integrate/unify/translate different IDLs, and provide tools and methods to facilitate system integration using popular IPC/RPC protocols, and a variety of deployment technologies.","In addition, IFEX defines a Interface Model (and its associated YAML syntax = IDL), which can be optionally used as a one-and-all source format for interface definitions. The flexible core model together with the strong Composable Layers design makes it a strong candidate for being the most capable interface description approach available. However, using the translation tools does not in itself require accepting the IFEX \"IDL\" as the unifying format."],"features":["Specifications and documentation"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/COVESA/ifex/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"604c0236d11a986224a82ce37b524b42f0ee94d1f8facb339b3aa7cf903fac37","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.586Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:15:43.586Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"...for the the Interface Exchange f